FINDINGS SUMMARY — canary_audit_and_breadth_tiering
====================================================================================================

PART A: SPY+TIP CANARY STATE FORWARD PREDICTIVE POWER
------------------------------------------------------
State distribution (Full 2001-2026, 297 months):
  both_pos 57.2% | spy_only 18.9% | tip_only 16.2% | both_neg 7.7%

Key result: both_pos has materially BETTER forward returns than other states.
  SPY fwd 1mo:  both_pos +1.26%  spy_only +0.03%  tip_only +0.35%  both_neg +0.89%
  FCP15_EW:     both_pos +1.28%  vs rest   +0.32%  =>  +0.96pp lift, hit rate 74% vs 58%
  SPY intra-DD: both_pos -2.94%  vs tip_only -6.26%  both_neg -6.90%

Interpretation:
  - both_pos = safest AND highest-return state. Forward return lift is real.
  - spy_only months (SPY up, TIP down) = WORST for forward returns (+0.03% mean).
    TIP's role: filtering out bearish-bond / high-SPY months with poor risk/reward.
  - tip_only months (DEFENSIVE in production) show +1.94% fwd SPY in live window.
    These ARE false-defensive calls on return, but SPY_maxDD=-6.26% confirms elevated
    intra-month risk. Canary correctly reads volatility even when end-month return is OK.
  - both_neg: highest intra-DD (-6.90%), correctly identified as most dangerous state.
  VERDICT: both_pos IS a distinct and superior state. But the improvement (+1.26% vs +0.89%)
  is not dramatic enough to justify concentration — variance matters as much as mean.

PART B: ALTERNATIVE CANARY SETS — RANKED BY SHARPE (Live 18y)
---------------------------------------------------------------
  Rank  Config                       Sharpe   CAGR%   MaxDD%    RO%
  1.    SPY+TIP (current)            +1.204   +9.99   -10.72   60.1%  ← WINNER
  2.    SPY 6mo SMA                  +1.082   +9.99   -22.53   76.5%
  3.    SPY alone (13612W)           +1.074  +10.13   -22.53   80.3%
  4.    SPY+VEA+EEM+AGG+TIP (3of5)  +1.035   +9.35   -18.07   71.8%
  5.    SPY+VEA+EEM+AGG (3-of-4)    +0.972   +8.53   -18.14   64.3%
  6.    SPY+VEA+EEM+AGG (4-of-4)    +0.821   +6.25   -16.65   44.6%
  7.    GLD+TLT (2-of-2)            +0.381   +2.57   -19.95   37.6%

  A. SPY+TIP is best on BOTH Sharpe AND MaxDD. Not close. No alternative beats it.
  B. TIP is the key: SPY alone Sh=1.074, MaxDD=-22.53% → adding TIP: Sh=+0.13, MaxDD halved.
     TIP captures bond-market stress that SPY momentum alone misses. Irreplaceable.
  C. VAA4 canaries are WORSE: 3-of-4 Sh=0.972 (-0.232 vs SPY+TIP), MaxDD=-18.14%.
     International/bond canaries create false defensives in US-dominated bull runs.
  D. GLD+TLT is useless as canary (DEF_hit%=31% — defensive calls wrong 69% of the time).
  VERDICT: Keep SPY+TIP. All tested alternatives are strictly inferior.

PART C: BREADTH TIERING — VERDICT
-----------------------------------
  Live-18y:
  Binary-Current (SPY+TIP)      Sh=+1.204  CAGR=+9.99%  MaxDD=-10.72%  ← BEST (by far)
  Binary-VAA4-Maj (3-of-4)      Sh=+0.972  CAGR=+8.53%  MaxDD=-18.14%
  Tiered-Standard (5-level)     Sh=+0.723  CAGR=+6.93%  MaxDD=-18.32%
  Tiered-VolVar (b4=TV20)       Sh=+0.538  CAGR=+6.16%  MaxDD=-27.15%  ← WORST

  Tiering hypothesis verdict: REJECTED. -0.481 Sharpe vs Binary-Current. Three penalties:
  (a) VAA4 canary weaker than SPY+TIP (demonstrated in Part B).
  (b) Breadth-4=top-1 concentration: eliminates pair diversification at 44.6% of months.
      Pair's low-correlation property is core to FCP resilience. Single asset kills Sharpe.
  (c) Breadth-1/2 partial exposure: losing money in crises without adequate protection.

  "All canaries positive = safe to concentrate" is empirically FALSE:
  Both_pos months do have better forward returns (Part A: +1.26% vs +0.35-0.89%).
  But the improvement is not large enough to justify the idiosyncratic risk of top-1.
  Variance of top-1 >> variance of min-vol pair. Risk-adjusted return drops sharply.

  Tiered TV=0.20 on breadth-4 makes things dramatically worse: MaxDD=-27.15%.
  Higher concentration + higher leverage = 2.5x drawdown amplification. Avoid.

ACTIONABLE CONCLUSIONS:
  1. Keep SPY+TIP canary as-is. Do not replace with VAA-style 4-asset canary.
  2. Do not implement breadth tiering. Binary on/off is optimal for this engine.
  3. Do not concentrate into top-1, even at full-conviction breadth-4. Pair beats single.
  4. Do not use higher TARGET_VOL when all canaries positive. DD cost is too high.
  5. The "full conviction = lever/concentrate" intuition is not supported by evidence.
  6. TIP's canary contribution is empirically proven and irreplaceable. Protect this.
  7. Paths to more CAGR: higher TV in binary structure (not concentration/tiering),
     universe additions, or PP_BLEND reduction — not canary redesign.
